  "notes": "Modified cash basis city (recorded as cash basis). Governmental lines from the Governmental Funds Statement of Receipts, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p5, Total Governmental Funds column); Golf, Housing, CDBG and Street are governmental funds. Beginning cash is not printed (only fund balances 1,142,344 -> 1,126,073); ending_cash is the sum of the cash lines on the governmental funds balance sheet (p4). Fund balances include receivables 78,950 and notes receivable offset by deferred revenues. Transfers are printed net per fund; transfers_in/out are the positive/negative fund columns (net (76,985) to the Utilities Fund). Business-type lines come from the government-wide modified cash Statement of Activities (pp2-3): utilities 412,043, charges 449,022, interest 1,601, miscellaneous 805, transfers 76,985, net position 269,177 -> 385,547. The accrual Proprietary Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7; net position 1,244,338 -> 1,395,368, incl. depreciation 61,090) and Proprietary Statement of Net Position (p6; total assets 1,416,388 incl. capital assets 988,453, liabilities 21,020) are on a different basis and not used for statement or detail lines. proprietary filled from the cash flow statement (p8). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p4, totals equal the government-wide figures), business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9, unaudited), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement plus the Utilities Fund from the modified cash Statement of Activities. 'Other Taxes' 400,922 has no printed breakdown by tax type. Governmental identity: 1,142,344 + 1,617,849 - 1,557,135 + 237,062 - 314,047 = 1,126,073. Business identity: 269,177 + 451,428 - 412,043 + 76,985 = 385,547. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
